 <p>Those questions need different evidence. A technical test can show that an assistant retrieves relevant information. It cannot, on its own, show whether people understand when to use it, whether they can challenge an answer, or whether reviewing the output is worth their time.</p>
 <p>My starting point for an adoption conversation is to examine the distance between the demonstration and an ordinary working day.</p>
 
